Use io and string.

Define function roman_value taking c as a byte returning a whole number:
    If c equals 73, give back 1.
    If c equals 86, give back 5.
    If c equals 88, give back 10.
    If c equals 76, give back 50.
    If c equals 67, give back 100.
    If c equals 68, give back 500.
    If c equals 77, give back 1000.
    Give back 0.
Done.

Define function roman_total taking text as a pointer to TcString returning a whole number:
    Let n be length of text.
    Let total start at 0.
    For every i from 0 as an unsigned number to n - 1:
        Let value be roman_value(text.data[i]).
        If i + 1 is less than n:
            Let next value be roman_value(text.data[i + 1]).
            If value is less than next value:
                Subtract value from total.
            Otherwise:
                Add value to total.
        Otherwise:
            Add value to total.
    Give back total.
Done.

Let first be str_from_bytes(bytes_ptr("MCMXCIV"), bytes_len("MCMXCIV")).
Let second be str_from_bytes(bytes_ptr("LVIII"), bytes_len("LVIII")).
Let third be str_from_bytes(bytes_ptr("IX"), bytes_len("IX")).
Say roman_total(address of first).
Say roman_total(address of second).
Say roman_total(address of third).
str_free(address of first).
str_free(address of second).
str_free(address of third).
Return 0.
